Kind: widen
Issue: #762
Holds open: both ways the klog forwarder loses bytes, on purpose -- char_server goes into the x86-64 bundle (OSFMK_BUILD_CHAR_SERVER is off by default, so nothing else runs the forwarder); before its first read the forwarder floods the ring with 320 numbered lines, about 71 KB against a 64 KiB ring, so the kernel moves its cursor; and the first write after the flood is refused as a tty would refuse it. The flood's last line and the refusal's announcement open run-x86_64.sh's two #762 pairs, which close on the lines saying what was lost.
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 1

diff --git a/uros/cmake/presets/x86_64.cmake b/uros/cmake/presets/x86_64.cmake
index 1301c825..aab06029 100644
--- a/uros/cmake/presets/x86_64.cmake
+++ b/uros/cmake/presets/x86_64.cmake
@@ -12,3 +12,6 @@ set(UROS_TARGET_ARCH x86_64 CACHE STRING "")
 # Release turns the kernel symbol table off by default; every build the harness
 # has judged had it on.
 set(OSFMK_GEN_KSYMS ON CACHE BOOL "")
+
+# 762-widen: char_server in the bundle, so that the klog forwarder runs.
+set(OSFMK_BUILD_CHAR_SERVER ON CACHE BOOL "")
